Fix 0012 backfill: handle legacy method_name NOT NULL + is_default NOT NULL

The legacy invoice_payment_methods schema has:
- method_name TEXT NOT NULL  (legacy column)
- is_default BOOLEAN         (no default, must be supplied)

Both blocks the backfill INSERT. Updated BLOCK 4 / 0012 to:
1. Drop NOT NULL on method_name (in a tolerant BEGIN/EXCEPTION block).
2. SET DEFAULT false on is_default (also tolerant).
3. Use a row-by-row loop so any other unexpected NOT NULL constraint
   skips the row instead of failing the whole batch and prints a
   NOTICE with the row's invoice_id, gateway, SQLSTATE, and SQLERRM.
4. Mirror payment_method into method_name so legacy code that still
   reads method_name keeps working.

tsc --noEmit: 0 errors. Backfill was simulated locally and now
includes all NOT NULL columns from the legacy schema.
